cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FactLens in your work, please cite it."
title: "FactLens: Decodability vs. Causality of Factual Recall in Small Language Models"
type: software
authors:
  - name: Cathy Li
repository-code: "https://github.com/CathyKernel/FactLens-Decodability-vs.-Causality-of-Factual-Recall-in-Small-Language-Models/tree/main/factlens"
url: "https://github.com/CathyKernel/FactLens-Decodability-vs.-Causality-of-Factual-Recall-in-Small-Language-Models"
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch interpretability toolkit for studying where small language
  models store and use factual knowledge: logit lens trajectories, linear
  probes with Hewitt-Liang control tasks, activation patching, and ROME-style
  causal tracing, synthesized into the Causal-Probe Gap (CPG) — the site-level
  disagreement between what is decodable and what is causal.
keywords:
  - interpretability
  - mechanistic-interpretability
  - language-models
  - probing
  - activation-patching
  - logit-lens
  - factual-recall
